Let me walk through the entire flow from start to finish:
1. Dealer Gets Onboarded
First, a dealer can't just sell - they must register and get approved. The dealer fills in business details (GST, PAN, address) on the signup screen, verifies their email via OTP, and sets a password. The backend creates a User (with is_active=False) and a Dealer record (with access_status='pending'). They can't do anything yet.
An Admin logs in and sees pending dealers under "Dealer Approvals". They review the documents and either Approve (sets is_approved=True, access_status='active') or Reject (records reason). Once approved, the dealer gets an email and can now log in.
2. Dealer Adds a Product
The dealer logs in, goes to "Add New Product", and fills out:
- Name, description, category, brand, images
- Prices: MRP, Selling Price, Dealer Price
- Attributes (like color, size, RAM - these are dynamic based on category)
- Variants (e.g., iPhone 14 in 128GB Black and 256GB Blue)
- Stock quantity, return policy, HSN code
When they submit, the backend:
- Validates the category exists
- Recursively walks up the category tree to find all mandatory attributes
- Checks every mandatory attribute is provided
- Auto-assigns the dealer's ID
- Creates the product with is_approved=False
- Creates variants as child products linked to the parent
The product appears in the dealer's list as "Pending Approval". Customers can't see it yet.
3. Admin Approves the Product
An Admin reviews pending products in their dashboard. They see the product details, images, pricing. They can either:
- Approve: Sets is_approved=True. The product now appears in search results, category pages - visible to all customers.
- Reject: Records a reason (e.g., "incorrect pricing"). The dealer sees this and can edit+resubmit.
Visibility rules: Public endpoints only show products where is_approved=True AND the dealer is active AND not deleted.
4. Customer Discovers & Buys
A customer (logged in via OTP or browsing as guest) finds the product through search or categories. They:
- Select variants (size/color)
- Add to cart → POST /api/v1/cart
- View cart, adjust quantities
- Proceed to checkout
Checkout is the most complex step - a single POST /api/v1/orders call does ALL this:
a) Validate cart items are still available (dealer active, approved)
b) Check stock for each item (variant stock or main stock)
c) Calculate price = selling_price ?? mrp ?? dealer_price
d) Calculate TAX:
   - Same state as dealer → CGST (9%) + SGST (9%) = 18%
   - Different state → IGST (18%)
e) Add platform fee (flat ₹X per item, set by dealer)
f) Calculate delivery charge (flat fee per dealer, waived if above free threshold)
g) Apply coupon if provided (validates: active, not expired, min order, usage limit)
h) Deduct wallet balance if opted
i) Deduct stock from the best-stocked hub's inventory
j) Create ONE ORDER PER CART ITEM (each item is its own order)
k) For each order: create OrderItem, generate Invoice, Tax Ledger entry
l) If customer was referred → create ReferralCommission (PENDING)
m) Clear the cart
n) Send email + in-app notification
5. Payment
The customer pays:
- COD: No upfront payment. Rider collects cash on delivery.
- Online (mock): Initiate payment → confirm with test card/UPI
- 4111111111111111 → Success
- success@upi → Success
On success: Payment.status = SUCCESS, Order.status = CONFIRMED
6. Dealer Fulfills the Order
The dealer sees the order in their dashboard and moves it through the status pipeline:
ORDER_PLACED → CONFIRMED → PROCESSING → PACKAGING → PACKED
→ DISPATCHED → SHIPPED → AT_HUB → OUT_FOR_DELIVERY → DELIVERED
Each status update notifies the customer. At "PACKED" stage, the order gets assigned to a hub. The hub staff assigns a rider. The rider delivers and marks it "DELIVERED".
On DELIVERED:
- delivered_at timestamp recorded
- Referral commission (if any) moves from PENDING → CREDITED
- Money added to referrer's wallet
7. Cancellation (Before Delivery)
Customer can cancel only if the order hasn't been shipped (status must be PENDING through PACKED).
When cancelled:
- Order status → CANCELLED
- Stock restored back to the product
- Coupon usage reversed (coupon can be used again)
- Refund initiated if payment was online (payment.status → REFUNDED)
- No refund for COD (no money taken)
- Referral commission → CANCELLED
8. Return or Exchange (After Delivery)
Customer has 7 days from delivery to request a return/exchange.
Return Request: Customer selects the item, provides reason + optional images, marks if it's an exchange.
The backend:
- Validates order is DELIVERED and within 7 days
- Creates OrderReturn with status REQUESTED
- Notifies admin/dealer
Admin or Dealer approves (dealer can only approve their own products):
For Returns:
- If online payment: refund is processed
- Admin provides UTR number → money returned to customer's original method
- Payment.status → REFUNDED
- If COD: no refund (customer already kept the cash)
- Order status → RETURNED
For Exchanges (more complex):
1. Verifies new variant/product has stock
2. Calculates price difference (extra to collect if new item is costlier)
3. Creates a replacement order with number like EXC-A3B8K2M1
4. Replacement order is auto-confirmed (status = CONFIRMED)
5. New OrderItem created with status = "packaging" (skips queue)
6. Stock deducted for replacement
7. Original order → RETURNED
Pickup flow: After approval:
APPROVED → OUT_FOR_PICKUP → PICKED_UP → COMPLETED/REFUNDED
For exchanges, the replacement order is delivered separately through normal flow.
If rejected: Admin records reason, status → REJECTED, customer is notified.
9. Super Admin's Role
Super Admin sits above everyone. They can do everything an Admin does, plus:
- Manage Partners (the organizations that dealers/helpdesk belong to)
- Create/delete any user including other super admins
- Access all system configurations
Regular Admin manages dealers & products. Super Admin manages the platform itself.




