For this massive analysis scope, "Graphify" is not a known tool in this environment. I'll proceed with a complete manual analysis using all available tools. Here is the comprehensive project analysis:
COMPLETE PROJECT ANALYSIS: Ecom_Backend_API (FastAPI E-commerce)
PHASE 1 – PROJECT DISCOVERY
Overall Architecture
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        FastAPI Application                          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  main.py (Entry Point)                                              │
│  ├── CORS Middleware (Allow: localhost:8081,8080,3000, *)          │
│  ├── SlowAPI Rate Limiter                                          │
│  ├── Static Files (/uploads)                                        │
│  ├── Request Validation Error Handler                               │
│  └── Startup Events (Schema sync, Support Escalation Loop)         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  Routers (31 files) → Prefix /api/v1                               │
│  Models (40+ tables) → SQLAlchemy async                             │
│  Schemas (20+ files) → Pydantic validation                         │
│  Services (7 files) → Business logic                                │
│  Core (7 files) → Config, DB, Security, Permissions                │
│  Modules: auction/, b2b_auction/                                    │
│  Migrations: SQL migration files                                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
Tech Stack
- Framework: FastAPI (Python 3.10+)
- ORM: SQLAlchemy 2.0 async with asyncpg
- Auth: JWT (HS256) + Argon2 password hashing + OTP-based customer auth
- Database: PostgreSQL (onlineshopappdb)
- Rate Limiting: SlowAPI
- Email: fastapi-mail (SMTP Gmail)
- File Validation: Pillow
- PDF Generation: Custom in services/invoice_pdf.py
