PHASE 3 – AUTHENTICATION (All Workflows)
1. Customer OTP Login
Screen: Customer Login Screen
→ POST /api/v1/auth/customer/login-request  (auth.py:170)
  Body: { identifier: "9876543210" }
  → Check CustomerUser exists + is_active
  → Generate 6-digit OTP, save to customer.otp_code
  → Send via SMS/Email
  → Response: { message: "OTP sent", temp_otp: otp }
  
→ POST /api/v1/auth/customer/login-verify  (auth.py:197)
  Body: { identifier: "9876543210", otp: "123456", full_name: "..." }
  → Verify OTP (or test codes "123456"/"654321")
  → Clear OTP, generate JWT { sub: identifier, is_customer: true }
  → Response: { access_token, token_type, user }
2. Customer Registration (OTP)
Screen: Register Screen
→ POST /api/v1/auth/customer/register-request (auth.py:92)
  Body: { identifier: phone }
  → Create pending CustomerUser (is_active=False) if new, else update OTP
  → Send OTP via SMS
  → Response: { message: "OTP sent", temp_otp }
  
→ POST /api/v1/auth/customer/register-verify (auth.py:129)
  Body: { identifier, otp, full_name }
  → Verify OTP, set full_name, set is_active=True, clear OTP
  → Generate JWT
  → Response: { access_token, token_type, user }
3. Staff Login (All roles: Admin/Dealer/Rider/Hub/Showroom/Logistics/Helpdesk)
Screen: [Role]LoginScreen
→ POST /api/v1/auth/login (auth.py:55)
  Body: { identifier: email/phone, password }
  → Look up user in users table (with dealer + partner eager load)
  → Verify password (Argon2)
  → Check: not CUSTOMER (must use OTP), is_active, partner.is_active, dealer checks
  → JWT: { sub: email/phone, role: role.value, is_customer: false }
  → Response: { access_token, token_type, user }
4. Dealer Registration
→ POST /auth/send-otp (auth.py:290) → OTP to email/phone
→ POST /auth/verify-otp (auth.py:325) → Verify + clear OTP
→ POST /auth/dealer-register (auth.py:338)
  Body: DealerSelfRegistration (business_name, gst, pan, address, owner_name, phone, password)
  → Update user: full_name, phone, password_hash, is_active=True
  → Create Dealer (is_approved=False, access_status='pending')
  → Auto-create default DeliveryHub ("Primary Warehouse")
  → Response: user object
5. Dealer Approval (Admin)
→ PUT /api/v1/admin/dealers/{id}/approve (admin.py:650)
  → Set Dealer.is_approved=True, access_status='active', profile_status='completed'
  → Auto-create hub if missing
  → Email notification: "Your dealer account is approved"
6. Account Reactivation
→ POST /auth/reactivate-request (auth.py:248) → OTP sent
→ POST /auth/verify-reactivation (auth.py:272)
  → Set is_active=True, deleted_at=None, clear OTP
7. Forgot/Change Password
→ POST /auth/send-otp → OTP to email
→ POST /auth/verify-otp → Verify
→ POST /auth/set-dealer-password (auth.py:404) → Update password_hash
PHASE 4 – BUSINESS WORKFLOWS
Customer Workflow
Browse → Search → View Product → Add to Cart → Checkout → Pay → Track → Receive → Return (if needed)
Key endpoints:
- GET /products (public) → GET /products/search?q= → GET /products/{id}
- POST /cart → GET /cart → PATCH /cart/{id} → DELETE /cart/{id}
- POST /orders → Creates 1 Order per cart item, deducts stock, initiates referral commissions
- POST /payments/initiate → POST /payments/{id}/confirm
- GET /orders → POST /orders/{id}/cancel
- POST /orders/{id}/return (within 7 days of delivery)
Order Status Pipeline
ORDER_PLACED → CONFIRMED → PROCESSING → PACKAGING → PACKED → DISPATCHED → SHIPPED → AT_HUB → OUT_FOR_DELIVERY → DELIVERED
                                                                                                              → CANCELLED (any point before SHIPPED)
                                                                                                              → RETURNED (after DELIVERED, within 7 days)
Dealer Workflow
Register → Wait Approval → Login → Dashboard → Add Products → Wait Approval → Manage Orders → Fulfill → Get Paid
Key dealer endpoints:
- GET /dealers/dashboard/stats → Status counts, total sales, products, rating
- GET /dealers/orders → Paginated orders with filters (status, date, search, hub, type)
- GET /dealers/orders/{id} → Order detail
- PUT /dealers/orders/{id}/status → Update status (dealer side)
- GET /dealers/hubs → List hubs
- GET /dealers/available-riders → List riders
- POST /dealers/discounts → Flash sales/discounts
- GET /dealers/team → Manage team members
- GET /dealers/inventory → Inventory management
Tax Calculation Workflow (in services/tax_service.py)
For each cart item during checkout:
1. Find TaxRule (priority: product-specific → category-level → parent category → default 0%)
2. Load TaxCategory (cgst_rate, sgst_rate, igst_rate)
3. Determine is_inter_state (buyer_state != seller_state)
4. total_rate = igst_rate if inter-state else cgst_rate + sgst_rate
5. taxable_amount = gross_value / (1 + total_rate/100) [price is inclusive]
6. total_tax = gross_value - taxable_amount
7. Split: IGST (if inter-state) or CGST=SGST=total_tax/2 (if intra-state)
8. Store in: Order, OrderItem, TaxLedger (audit trail)
Referral Commission Workflow
1. Customer registers with referral code → CustomerReferralProfile.referred_by_id set
2. Order placed → ReferralOrderCommission + ReferralItemCommission created (status=PENDING)
3. Order DELIVERED → core/order_status_logic.py:settle_referral_commissions_for_order()
   → Commission status → CREDITED
   → CustomerWallet.available_balance += commission_amount
   → WalletTransaction (CREDIT) created
4. Order CANCELLED → Commission status → CANCELLED
Return/Exchange Workflow
Customer → POST /orders/{id}/return (status=REQUESTED)
    → Admin/Dealer → POST /admin/returns/{id}/approve
        → status=APPROVED, refund calculation
        → if ONLINE payment: refund_mode, optional refund_reference (UTR)
        → if EXCHANGE: Creates replacement order (EXC-xxxx), stock deducted
    → Admin → PUT /admin/returns/{id}/process-refund (finalize with UTR)
    → Admin → POST /admin/returns/{id}/reject (status=REJECTED)

Return Status Flow: REQUESTED → APPROVED → OUT_FOR_PICKUP → PICKED_UP → COMPLETED/REFUNDED
Exchange Flow: APPROVED → OUT_FOR_PICKUP → PICKED_UP → OUT_FOR_SWAP → SWAP_COMPLETED → EXCHANGE_COMPLETED
PHASE 5 – API TRACE (All Routes)
Method	Route	Router	Auth	Description
POST	/api/v1/auth/register	auth.py	5/min	Register staff user
POST	/api/v1/auth/login	auth.py	5/min	Staff login
