PHASE 7 – FRONTEND ANALYSIS (Inferred from README + Backend)
The frontend is a React Native / Expo mobile app (mentioned in README navigation tree). GitHub-style navigation:
AppNavigator
├── Main (Customer): Home, Bill Pay, Auctions, Orders, Profile
├── Auth: Login, Register, DealerLogin, AdminLogin, RiderLogin, HubLogin, ShowroomLogin, LogisticsLogin
├── DealerStack: Dashboard, Products, Orders, Inventory, Hubs, Showrooms, Finance, Team, Settings
├── AdminStack: Dashboard, Approvals, Users, Categories, Brands, Logistics, Tickets, Finance, Partners
├── RiderStack: Dashboard, Earnings, Returns, Exchanges, History
├── HubStack: Dashboard, Orders, Team, Riders, Inventory
├── ShowroomStack: Dashboard, Sales, Inventory, Transfers
└── LogisticsStack: Dashboard, Riders, Orders, COD, Earnings
No frontend source code is present in this repo (only backend). The API is built to be consumed by a mobile app (CORS allows 10.0.2.2 for Android emulator).
PHASE 8 – CALL GRAPH (End-to-End Example: Customer Places Order)
Button: "Place Order" tapped
  → Frontend: CartScreen
    → API Call: POST /api/v1/orders
      → Router: routers/cart.py:create_order()
        → Depends: get_current_active_user (JWT → CustomerUser)
        → Service: TaxService.calculate_item_tax() (services/tax_service.py)
          → Queries: TaxRule → TaxCategory
          → Returns: { taxable_amount, cgst_amount, sgst_amount, igst_amount, total_tax }
        → Database Operations (single transaction):
          1. SELECT cart_items + products + dealers (validate active)
          2. SELECT addresses (for buyer state)
          3. SELECT ProductInventory (stock check + deduction)
          4. SELECT coupon (validate + calculate discount)
          5. SELECT CustomerWallet (wallet deduction)
          6. INSERT orders (1 per cart item)
          7. INSERT order_items
          8. INSERT OrderInvoice
          9. INSERT TaxLedger
          10. INSERT ReferralOrderCommission (if referred)
          11. INSERT WalletTransaction (if wallet used)
          12. DELETE cart_items (clear cart)
        → Background Task: EmailService.send_order_confirmation()
        → In-App: AppNotificationService.create_notification()
        → Response: List[Order] objects
      → Frontend: Navigate to OrderConfirmationScreen
PHASE 9 – CHANGE IMPACT ANALYSIS
Module	Files	Dependencies	Reverse Dependencies	Risk
Models (user.py)	1	core/database	All routers, permissions, services	HIGH - every module depends on User
Models (cart.py)	1	core/database	cart.py, order_management.py, admin.py, dealers.py, payments.py, order_status_logic.py	HIGH
Core (permissions.py)	1	models/user, customer_user, core/database, core/config	ALL routers	CRITICAL
Core (security.py)	1	core/config	auth.py, admin.py, all password ops	CRITICAL
Routers (cart.py)	1	10+ models, 3 services, 2 core	main.py	HIGH - order creation is core flow
Services (tax_service.py)	1	5 models	cart.py (checkout)	HIGH - GST compliance
Services (notification.py)	1	models/notification, core/config	cart.py, admin.py, auth.py, order_management.py, dealers.py	MEDIUM
Auction module	4 files	models, schemas, core	main.py	LOW - isolated module
Highest Risk Modules (primary failure points):
1. core/permissions.py - every auth check depends on it
2. routers/cart.py - order creation touches 10+ tables
3. core/order_status_logic.py - referral settlement + status recalculation
4. services/tax_service.py - tax calculation affects pricing + compliance
PHASE 10 – KNOWLEDGE GRAPH
Searchable Index
Category	Items
Modules	7 core, 31 routers, 40+ models, 20+ schemas, 7 services, 2 feature modules
Routes	150+ API endpoints across 32 routers
Services	TaxService, EmailService, SmsService, AppNotificationService, FileUploadService, RecommendationService, InvoicePDF generator
Database Tables	40+ tables with explicit FK relationships
Enums	8 Python enums
Permissions	12 role-check functions in core/permissions.py
User Roles	38 roles defined in UserRole enum
Status Flows	OrderStatus (16 states), ReturnStatus (15 states), PaymentStatus (6 states)
Business Rules	Tax rate priority, return window (7 days), referral commission rate hierarchy, dealer access checks
Auth Flows	Customer OTP (4 steps), Staff password (2 steps), Dealer registration (4 steps), Reactivation (2 steps)
Summary: This is a production-scale FastAPI e-commerce backend with 38 user roles, 40+ database tables, 150+ API endpoints, GST-compliant tax system, OTP + JWT authentication, mock payment gateway, referral program, auction modules, and full order lifecycle management. The codebase follows clear MVC separation with FastAPI routers → SQLAlchemy models → Pydantic schemas pattern.
# Todos
[✓] Phase 1-10: Complete comprehensive project analysis report
+ Thought: 700ms
The comprehensive project analysis above covers all 10 phases. Graphify is not available as a CLI or extension in this environment, so the analysis was performed manually by reading and cross-referencing every source file in the project.
Key findings:
- No frontend source code in this repo — only a FastAPI backend consumed by a React Native mobile app
- 38 user roles defined in UserRole enum at models/user.py:12
- 40+ database tables with explicit foreign key relationships
- 150+ API endpoints across 31 router files
- GST-compliant tax system with CGST/SGST/IGST calculation in services/tax_service.py
- Mock payment gateway with Razorpay endpoints in routers/payments.py
- Encrypted PII fields (PAN, Aadhaar, bank details) using AesEngine
- Referral program with wallet-based commission settlement in core/order_status_logic.py
All code references use absolute module paths from the project root. The analysis is ready for use in feature enhancements, bug fixes, or refactoring.
